REPRO (temp board)
  karr archive 4 99   # only 4 processed, 99 silently dropped, exit 0
  karr archive 4,99   # comma form works: 4 archived, 99 warned, exit 1
  karr show 1 2       # shows 1, the 2 is silently dropped

Batch commands take ONE comma-separated positional; everything after it is
ignored without any diagnostic. kanban-md accepts space-separated ID lists
(cobra runBatch over args) — an agent typing `karr archive 4 5 6` believes
all three are archived when only 4 was.

FIX DIRECTION: either accept space-separated IDs like the reference (join
remaining positionals) or reject extra args loudly. Same family as task #5
(silent CLI misbehavior).

